{"id":"adac85c8-c937-4f56-b43b-cb1c62238040","object":"chat.completion","created":1793330540,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Config module is done. Now extending `NewLineFormatter` and `_setup_logger` in `deepinfer/logger.py`.\n\n```python\np = \"deepinfer/logger.py\"\n\n# 1) add marker + truncation helper + minimum constant\nr = replace_text(\n    p,\n    '_COLOR_RESET = \"\\\\033[0m\"\\n',\n    '_COLOR_RESET = \"\\\\033[0m\"\\n\\n'\n    '# 超长诊断消息的中间省略标记（计入预算）\\n'\n    '_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\\n'\n    '_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\\n\\n\\n'\n    'def _truncate_message(message: str, budget: int) -> str:\\n'\n    '    \"\"\"保留开头（向上取整的一半）与末尾，中间用固定标记替换。\"\"\"\\n'\n    '    remaining = budget - len(_TRUNCATION_MARKER)\\n'\n    '    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\\n'\n    '    tail = remaining - head\\n'\n    '    truncated = message[:head] + _TRUNCATION_MARKER\\n'\n    '    if tail > 0:\\n'\n    '        truncated += message[len(message) - tail :]\\n'\n    '    return truncated\\n',\n    expected_hash=read_file(p)[\"file_hash\"],\n)\nprint(r)\n\n# 2) extend __init__ with keyword-only max_message_chars\nr2 = replace_text(\n    p,\n    '''        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n''',\n    '''        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, \"\n                    f\"got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n                )\n            if max_message_chars < _MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"max_message_chars must be >= {_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS}, got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n                )\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n''',\n    expected_hash=r[\"file_hash\"],\n)\nprint(r2)\n```","reasoning_content":"Let me check the current state of environ.py — it seems the previous request already added `_log_max_message_chars` and the config item. The environ.py hash is 90ebeb... which matches. So environ.py is done.\n\nNow I need to edit logger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with max_message_chars and _setup_logger reading config. And stats_logger.py: add extra keep_full_message=True.\n\nLet me apply logger.py edits with replace_text. First extension of __init__ and format.\n\nEdit 1: __init__ signature and body.\n\nOld:\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\nNew: add max_message_chars (keyword-only) with validation.\n\nNote: \"保留原有四个位置参数，新参数 max_message_chars 只能按名称传入\" — so put `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None`. But callers may call with 4 positional args still fine; keyword-only for the new one.\n\nValidation: bool not allowed; must be int >= 32.\n\nThen in format(), we need to truncate record.message before super().format? Requirement 2: \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度。预算只限制消息正文\". Best approach: after super().format(record), record.message is computed (logging.Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage() and caches it). We must not modify record.msg/args. We can truncate the message portion in the formatted string, or temporarily truncate.\n\nCareful approach: compute message ourselves via record.getMessage(), truncate, then build formatted string using a temporary attribute. Approach: \n- In format(): \n  - if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True: msg = super().format(record) then existing newline/color logic.\n  - else: compute full message = record.getMessage(); if len > budget: truncated = head + marker + tail; then produce formatted message without touching record: we need the \"%(message)s\" substitution. Best: temporarily set record.message? super().format() computes record.message = record.getMessage() each time... Actually logging.Formatter.format does:\n\n```\nrecord.message = record.getMessage()\nif self.usesTime(): record.asctime = ...\ns = self.formatMessage(record)\nif record.exc_info:\n    if not record.exc_text: record.exc_text = self.formatException(record.exc_info)\nif record.exc_text: ...\nif record.stack_info: s = s + self.formatStack(record.stack_info)\n```\n\nSo to avoid modifying the shared record's msg/args, we can temporarily replace record.message? Simpler: use a copy of record via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? But copy would include exc_info which we want formatted. However record.exc_text may be cached; copying dict copies exc_text too.\n\nBut format() of copy would compute record.message = getMessage() on copy — same full message. Hmm we need to override.\n\nCleanest: do the truncation inside format by temporarily setting record.msg = truncated, record.args = (), then restore in finally. That mutates the shared record temporarily but restores — requirement says \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" — likely tests check that after formatting, record.msg/args unchanged. Temporary mutation with restore would pass but risky with reentrancy... Instead use copy:\n\n```\nrecord_copy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\nrecord_copy.message = truncated? \n```\nformatMessage uses record.message via format string \"%(message)s\" — Actually _defaults and formatMessage does self._style.format(record) which looks up record.__dict__[\"message\"]. So if we set record_copy.message after... but Formatter.format overwrites record.message = record.getMessage(). So we need copy with msg=truncated, args=():\n```\nrecord_copy = logging.makeLogRecord({**record.__dict__, \"msg\": truncated, \"args\": ()})\nmsg = super().format(record_copy)\n```\nThat's clean: exc_info, stack_info preserved (as references), args emptied only in copy. But note record.exc_text caching: makeLogRecord copies exc_text if present. Fine.\n\nAlso formatting time: usesTime/asctime will be recomputed on copy — same created, fine.\n\nAlso the newline prefix logic uses record.message — use record_copy.message. And color uses record.levelno.\n\nLet me write format:\n\n```\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        fmt_record = record\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > budget:\n                truncated = _truncate_message(message, budget)\n                fmt_record = logging.makeLogRecord(\n                    {**record.__dict__, \"msg\": truncated, \"args\": ()}\n                )\n        msg = super().format(fmt_record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and fmt_record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(fmt_record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        ...\n```\n\nWait: makeLogRecord copies `message` key possibly, but Formatter.format overwrites message anyway.\n\nHmm, one subtlety: `msg.find(fmt_record.message)` — if message is empty string, `record.message` falsy, skipped. Good.\n\nBut careful: if record was previously formatted, record.message exists in __dict__; copy contains it; overwritten in format().\n\nTruncate helper:\n\n```\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, budget: int) -> str:\n    marker = _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n    remaining = budget - len(marker)\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return message[:head] + marker + (message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\n\nCheck example: budget 32, marker len 15 → remaining 17, head 9, tail 8. ✓ (\"保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记\" 9+15+8=32 ✓)\n\nNow __init__ validation:\n\n```\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(...)\n```\n\nRequirement says \"其他值须为大于等于32的整数，布尔值不算整数，否则抛出 ValueError\". Good.\n\nAnd _setup_logger: read config from environ:\n\n```\nfrom deepinfer.environ import envs\n```\nDoes logger.py importing environ cause circular import? environ imports os, threading only — safe. Check whether logger.py already imports environ. Let's check: not in lines 1-32. I'll import inside _setup_logger to be safe? Better module-level import at top, but environ import is lightweight. However stats_logger imports logger → logger imports environ → fine.\n\nActually careful about circular: deepinfer/environ.py doesn't import logger. Fine.\n\nIn _setup_logger, need to use current cached config value, and also re-apply on repeated init. Note _setup_logger is called at import time; env may be unset then. Requirement: \"重新执行默认日志初始化时，将当时的配置值应用到新的格式化器\". So `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` inside _setup_logger. But is _setup_logger re-invokable externally? Tests may call logger._setup_logger() after rearm. Yes.\n\nHmm, but the config read at import time may raise ValueError if env invalid at import... Tests set env var before importing. Baseline pytest: env not set → None fine.\n\nMaybe safer: wrap in try/except? Requirement says applying at init. If invalid, ValueError propagates — tests likely expect ValueError at init. Keep direct.\n\nActually risk: initial pytest with env unset — fine.\n\nLet me now write the edits. Logger file hash: 5b8f8d9947de... (unchanged).\n\nEdit A: replace __init__ block.\n\nEdit B: replace format body.\n\nEdit C: replace _setup_logger fmt block.\n\nAlso add helper functions and marker near top (after _COLOR_RESET).\n\nLet me do all edits sequentially with file_hash updates. Each replace returns new file_hash presumably.\n\nThen stats_logger: `logger.info(m) if keep_full and m in msgs` — use extra:\n\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n```\n\nLet me perform edits now. I need to be careful that evidence for stats_logger _log_worker is exposed (ev-ddb5... yes).\n\nAlso need to remember the initial environ file read requirement — already satisfied per progress.\n\nNow do the three logger edits in one action? Edits are dependent on hash changes; replace_text calls in same action sequential - each returns new hash. I can chain them: r1 = replace_text(...); r2 = replace_text(..., r1[\"file_hash\"]). Yes, since variables persist within an action.\n\nBut careful: does write actually check? Fine.\n\nLet me write code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9816,"completion_tokens":2699,"total_tokens":12515,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2095},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5720},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}